# LF in the index and LF in every working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference: git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so without
# this the windows-latest runner checks the tree out as CRLF. Biome formats to LF, which
# fails `just format-check`, and the justfile runs every recipe through bash, which
# cannot execute a CRLF script. Neither failure is reproducible on Linux or macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored screenshot font is binary; `text=auto` above detects that, and this says so
# outright so no future eol rule can be read as reaching it.
*.ttf -text

# Recorded GitHub responses, byte for byte as `gh api --include` printed them: their header
# lines end in CRLF, which is what the release-tail replay serves back.
.github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/recordings/*.http -text
.github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/recordings-v0.13.0/*.http -text
